      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Wood chips are small- to medium-sized pieces of wood formed by cutting or chipping larger pieces of wood such as trees, branches, logging residues, stumps, roots, and wood waste. They may be used as a biomass solid fuel and are raw material for producing wood pulp. They may also be used as an organic mulch in gardening, landscaping, and ecosystem restoration. Wood chips can provide a cushioned landing below swing sets and jungle gyms.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "木片是通过切割或削片大块的木头（如树木、树枝、伐木残余物、树桩、根和木材废料）形成的小到中等大小的木片。它们可以作为生物质固体燃料使用，也是生产木浆的原料。它们还可以用作园艺、园林景观和生态系统恢复中的有机覆盖物。木片可以在秋千和丛林健身房下方提供一个有弹性的着陆点。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
